                        <p><span style=3D"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)=
;color:rgb(0,0,0);"><span>Applicable Products: Notebook, Desktop, All-in-On=
e PC, Gaming Handheld</span></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The Cloud Recovery f=
unction allows you to restore your computer's operating system in just a fe=
w steps without installing drivers.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><img class=3D"image_=
resized" style=3D"width:61.8%;" src=3D"https://km-ap.asus.com/uploads2/Phot=
oLibrarys/b9f3f97c-3d96-4037-8f3a-78581227d1e2/20230511163651713_20230511_1=
60323.jpg"></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><iframe width=3D"1280" src=3D"cid:frame-F0EA=
29B058FB3A4B01984774EDB66A83@mhtml.blink" scrolling=3D"no" height=3D"720" f=
rameborder=3D"0" allowfullscreen=3D"" allow=3D"accelerometer; autoplay; enc=
rypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" data-gtm-yt-inspected-1710318_=
2772=3D"true" id=3D"954755359" data-gtm-yt-inspected-1710318_556=3D"true" d=
ata-gtm-yt-inspected-204=3D"true" data-gtm-yt-inspected-209=3D"true" title=
=3D"How to Use Cloud Recovery in UEFI?      | ASUS SUPPORT" data-dashlane-f=
rameid=3D"5532"></iframe></p><p>To provide you more detailed instruction, y=
ou can also click ASUS YouTube video link below to know more about How to u=
se Cloud Recovery in UEFI:</p><p><a href=3D"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=
=3DQDtthnHv4ik" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">https://www.y=
outube.com/watch?v=3DQDtthnHv4ik</a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><a name=3D"C10">Con=
tents</a></p><ol><li><a href=3D"https://rog.asus.com/us/support/faq/1048106=
/#C1">System Requirement</a></li><li><a href=3D"https://rog.asus.com/us/sup=
port/faq/1048106/#C2">How to enter the UEFI BIOS</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp=
;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&n=
bsp;&nbsp;<br>2.1 <a href=3D"https://rog.asus.com/us/support/faq/1048106/#C=
21">Consumer Notebook</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>2.2 <a hre=
f=3D"https://rog.asus.com/us/support/faq/1048106/#C22">Commercial Notebook\=
Desktops</a><a>\All-in-One PCs</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>2=
.3 <a href=3D"https://rog.asus.com/us/support/faq/1048106/#C23">Gaming Note=
book</a><a>\Gaming Desktops\ROG Ally</a></li><li><a>Execute the </a><a href=
=3D"https://rog.asus.com/us/support/faq/1048106/#C6">Cloud Recovery</a></li=
><li><a href=3D"https://rog.asus.com/us/support/faq/1048106/#C7">Cloud Reco=
very is not accessible</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbs=
p;<br>4.1 <a href=3D"https://rog.asus.com/us/support/faq/1048106/#C71">This=
 project does not support Cloud Recovery</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>4.2 <a href=3D"htt=
ps://rog.asus.com/us/support/faq/1048106/#C72">Device information is missin=
g</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbs=
p;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>4.3 <a href=3D"https://rog.asus.com/us/support/faq/104810=
6/#C73">No WiFi icon</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li><a href=3D"https://rog.a=
sus.com/us/support/faq/1048106/#C8">Q&amp;A</a></li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><a=
 name=3D"C1">1. System Requirement</a></p><ul><li>You can click <a href=3D"=
https://www.asus.com/support/cloud-recovery" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noope=
ner noreferrer">here </a>to find out if your Asus laptop supports Cloud Rec=
overy within UEFI BIOS</li><li>If the initial system is Windows 11 Home S m=
ode, this feature is not supported</li><li>ARM architecture (e.g. Qualcomm =
platform) laptops do not support this feature</li><li>Local backup&nbsp;req=
uires an external storage device</li><li>Cloud Recovery require LAN or Wi-F=
i network</li><li>Power supply</li></ul><p><a href=3D"https://rog.asus.com/=
us/support/faq/1048106/#C10">Back to Contents</a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><a nam=
e=3D"C2">2. How to enter the UEFI BIOS</a></p><p><span style=3D"color:rgb(2=
55,0,0);"><span>=E2=80=BB Before you start using the Cloud Recovery, please=
 fix the UEFI BIOS time. If UEFI BIOS time is not the current time, Cloud R=
